==============================================================================
Comparison vs task target leading constants
==============================================================================
  4/(3π) = 0.42441318157838758829
  2/(3π) = 0.21220659078919379414
  14/3   = 4.66666666666666696273

  |14/3 - 4/(3π)| = 4.2422534851e+00
  |14/3 - 2/(3π)| = 4.4544600759e+00
  Ratio (14/3)/(4/(3π)) = 10.9955742876  =  7π/2 = 10.9955742876

==============================================================================
VERDICT
==============================================================================

FAIL:  S4 chain (KMV §5 variance + KMV §4 mean + ILS §3 sign)
       does NOT close at c1 = 4/(3π) for the WEIGHT-aspect Petersson family.

Two structural mismatches against the task hypothesis c1 = 4/(3π) at log^4 X:
  1. The KMV §5 unmollified diagonal Mellin residue has leading power L^3,
     not L^4.  KMV (Crelle 2000) eq. (5) is verbatim:  Q^h ~ c'_k (log q̂)^{2k+1}.
     For k=1 (1st derivative, 2nd moment): power is (log q̂)^3.

  2. The leading L^3 rational coefficient is 14/3, off from 4/(3π) by 7π/2.

Power mismatch is *structural*, not *numerical*: no constant rescaling can
convert L^3 to L^4.  The CFKRS-recipe target c1·L^4 corresponds to the 4-shift
ratio recipe, which uses an additional integration step (the 'extra log factor
from L^2 expansion of L(1/2,f) on the even subfamily').  The unmollified KMV
§5 residue computes only the *direct* diagonal moment of |Λ'(f, 1/2)|^2.

Conclusion: the S4 sufficient-conditions chain in
    handoff-2026-05-04-theorem-B-and-C1/Weakest_sufficient_conditions.md
misattributes a (log N)^4 leading-order claim to KMV §5; the actual KMV §5
statement is (log q̂)^3 unmollified, (log q̂)^0 mollified.  In neither form does
KMV §5 alone deliver 2/(3π)·(log NkT)^4 unconditionally.
